Who are we?  It all starts with the mission: NVISO is here to protect European society from potentially devastating cyber attacks! This means we offer cyber security services to private and governmental organizations to help them better prepare for, prevent, detect and respond to cyber security incidents.  All of this is built on four fundamental values that define who we are: We are Proud, We Break Barriers, We Care and No BS!

What will you do?  You have strong background in managing large IT-Projects or Cybersecurity-Programs and believe the following to be applicable to you?

As a  Senior Program Manager in Cybersecurity

(m/w/d) ,  located in Germany , you will lead and manage complex, large-scale programs and projects for NVISO clients, with a strong focus on cybersecurity-related initiatives (e.g. security transformation programs, incident response engagements, security operations build-outs, compliance and regulatory programs, implementation of Business Continuity Management Systems and Disaster Recovery Programs). Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

Act as the primary point of contact for client stakeholders, building trusted relationships at both operational and executive level;

Define project scope, objectives, timelines, budgets, and resource plans, and ensure delivery within these constraints.

Coordinate cross-functional and multidisciplinary teams, including NVISO security consultants, engineers, and client-side teams;

Identify, track, and mitigate project and program risks, issues, and dependencies proactively.

Manage stakeholder communication, status reporting, and governance structures (steering committees, status meetings, escalation paths);

Support pre-sales activities where relevant, such as scoping engagements, estimating effort, and contributing to proposals;

Drive continuous improvement of program/project management practices within NVISO's delivery teams;

Ensure quality, compliance, and client satisfaction throughout the project/program lifecycle.

Requirements

You hold citizenship in one of the 32 NATO member states

or the Austrian citizenship;

Several years of proven experience (typically 7+ years) as a Program Manager or Senior Project Manager, ideally in IT, security consulting, or technology-driven environments;

Strong affinity for or demonstrable experience in cybersecurity - understanding of security concepts, terminology, and the challenges clients face (prior direct cybersecurity project experience is a plus, but not mandatory);

Solid knowledge of project/program management methodologies (e.g. PMP, Prince2, Agile/Scrum, SAFe) and ability to adapt approach to client context;

Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills - comfortable interacting with both technical teams and C-level client representatives;

Strong leadership skills with the ability to motivate and align diverse, often remote or multi-location teams;

